.TH VDF 1 "November 2026" "vdf 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vdf \- visual disk free: disk usage with colour-gradient bars
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdf
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vdf
reports free disk space like
.BR df (1)
with
.BR \-h ,
but it draws a horizontal colour-gradient bar for each entry.
.PP
By default the output is grouped by physical disk.
Each disk gets an \fBentire disk\fR row that shows how much of the physical media is used,
free, or unallocated (not covered by any partition).
The volumes mounted from that disk are listed underneath it.
Filesystems that are not backed by a local disk, such as network shares, are listed under \fBother\fR.
.PP
Each bar is scaled to the size of its row.
The gradient spans the full width of the bar, so a fuller entry reaches further into the warm colours.
A grey hatched segment marks space that the volume cannot use.
On macOS this is usually space taken by other APFS volumes in the same container.
On Linux it is usually space reserved for root.
A dotted segment marks unallocated space on a disk.
.PP
When one or more \fIPATH\fR arguments are given,
.B vdf
shows only the filesystems that contain them, as a flat list.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-disks
Show physical disks only, without volume rows.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-flat
Show a flat list of volumes, without grouping by disk (the classic df layout).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Include pseudo, hidden and duplicate filesystems, and disk images that have no visible volumes.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-long
Also show the device and the filesystem type.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-names
Show volume names (for example "Macintosh HD") instead of mount points.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-inodes
Show inode usage instead of block usage. Implies \fB\-\-flat\fR.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-si
Use powers of 1000 instead of 1024.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-local
Show local filesystems only.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-type " " \fITYPE\fR
Show only filesystems of this type. May be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exclude\-type " " \fITYPE\fR
Hide filesystems of this type. May be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-sort " " \fIKEY\fR
Sort volumes by \fBmount\fR, \fBsize\fR, \fBused\fR, \fBavail\fR or \fBpct\fR.
The default is system order.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reverse
Reverse the sort order.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-total
Add a grand-total row. Volumes that share a container or pool are counted once.
.TP
.BR \-\-theme " " \fINAME\fR
Gradient colours: \fBheat\fR (default), \fBocean\fR, \fBsunset\fR, \fBforest\fR, \fBrainbow\fR or \fBmono\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-color " " \fIWHEN\fR
\fBauto\fR (default), \fBalways\fR, \fBnever\fR, \fB256\fR or \fBtruecolor\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Draw the bars with plain ASCII characters.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width " " \fIN\fR
Total output width. The default is the terminal width.
.TP
.BR \-\-bar\-max " " \fIN\fR
Maximum bar width in columns (default 80).
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-name " " \fIN\fR
Maximum width of the name column (default 32).
.TP
.BR \-\-warn " " \fIPCT\fR
Flag usage at or above \fIPCT\fR percent with "!" (default 90).
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-header ", " \-\-no\-legend
Omit the header row or the legend.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print disks and volumes as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VDF_THEME
Default gradient theme.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colour when set.
.TP
.B COLORTERM
24-bit colour is used when this is set to \fBtruecolor\fR or \fB24bit\fR,
and 256 colours otherwise.
.TP
.B COLUMNS
Overrides the detected terminal width.
.SH NOTES
On macOS the \fBUsed\fR figure for an APFS volume is the space used by that volume
(\fBATTR_VOL_SPACEUSED\fR), the same figure that
.BR df (1)
shows.
Disk information comes from the IOKit registry.
On Linux it comes from \fI/sys/block\fR,
and device-mapper (LVM, LUKS) and md devices are followed back to their physical disks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if a path cannot be resolved or there is nothing to show.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B vdf
Disks and their volumes.
.TP
.B vdf \-d
Physical disks only.
.TP
.B vdf ~
The filesystem that holds your home directory.
.TP
.B vdf \-f \-s pct \-r
All volumes, fullest first.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR df (1),
.BR diskutil (8),
.BR lsblk (8)
.SH AUTHOR
jggonz and contributors. Source: https://github.com/jggonz/vdf
